@startuml
!theme plain
skinparam componentStyle rectangle
title Component Diagram – Peer Review System 

package "User Device" {
  component "Vue.js SPA\n(in Browser)" as FrontendApp
}

package "Kubernetes Cluster" {
  
  ' L'Ingress Controller è l'unico punto di ingresso e reverse proxy.
  component "Ingress Controller\n(NGINX)" as Ingress

  ' Questo Nginx serve solo i file statici, non fa più da proxy.
  component "Frontend Web Server\n(Nginx)" as FrontendWebServer

  package "Backend Microservices" {
    component "Authentication Service" as Auth
    component "Assignment Service" as Assignment
    component "Submission Service" as Submission
    component "Review Service" as Review
    component "Reporting Service" as Reporting
  }

  package "Data Stores" {
    database "PostgreSQL\n(Users)" as DBAuth
    database "MongoDB\n(Assignments)" as DBAssignment
    database "MongoDB\n(Submissions)" as DBSubmission
    database "MongoDB\n(Reviews)" as DBReview
    component "MinIO\n(Object Storage)" as MinIOStorage
  }
}


' === Flusso Utente e API ===
' L'utente nel browser fa due tipi di richieste, entrambe dirette all'Ingress.
FrontendApp --> Ingress : "1. GET / (Richiesta per la SPA)\n2. POST /auth/login (Richiesta API)\n(HTTPS/TLS)"


' L'Ingress instrada il traffico in base al path.
Ingress --> FrontendWebServer : "Route to Frontend (path: /)"
Ingress --> Auth : "Route to Auth Service (path: /auth/...)"
Ingress --> Assignment : "Route to Assignment Service (path: /assignments/...)"
Ingress --> Submission : "Route to Submission Service (path: /submissions/...)"
Ingress --> Review : "Route to Review Service (path: /reviews/...)"
Ingress --> Reporting : "Route to Reporting Service (path: /reports/...)"

FrontendWebServer --> FrontendApp : "Serves static files (HTML, JS, CSS)"


' === Accesso ai Database (invariato) ===
Auth --> DBAuth : SQL
Assignment --> DBAssignment : MongoDB Driver
Submission --> DBSubmission : MongoDB Driver
Review --> DBReview : MongoDB Driver


' === Interazioni con Object Storage (invariato) ===
Submission --> MinIOStorage : S3 API (HTTP)


' === Chiamate API Inter-Servizio (interne al cluster) ===
note as InterServiceNote
  **Inter-Service Communication:**
  Services communicate directly using
  Kubernetes service discovery
  (e.g., http://assignment-service/...).
end note
InterServiceNote .. Review
InterServiceNote .. Submission
InterServiceNote .. Reporting

Review -[#blue]-> Assignment : API HTTP
Review -[#blue]-> Submission : API HTTP
Submission -[#blue]-> Assignment : API HTTP
Reporting -[#blue]-> Assignment : API HTTP
Reporting -[#blue]-> Submission : API HTTP
Reporting -[#blue]-> Review : API HTTP


' === Dipendenze per Validazione JWT (invariato) ===
note right of Auth
  **JWT Validation:**
  Backend services validate JWTs
  by fetching the public key from
  the Auth service's `/public_key` endpoint.
end note
Assignment .[#green].> Auth : API HTTP (e.g. /public_key)
Submission .[#green].> Auth : API HTTP
Review .[#green].> Auth : API HTTP
Reporting .[#green].> Auth : API HTTP


note bottom of Ingress
  **Ingress Controller (Single Reverse Proxy):**
  - Acts as the single entry point for all external traffic.
  - Handles TLS termination.
  - Routes requests to the appropriate service
    (Frontend or Backend) based on the URL path.
end note

@enduml